INT. AFFINAGE CAVE - CHEESE VAULT - NIGHT

A limestone tunnel lined with wooden racks of aging wheels, each stamped with a date. Cool mist hangs in the lamplight. Water drips somewhere deep.

MARISKA DELACROIX-ODUYA (40s, white coat, hairnet) crouches at a rack with a cheese iron, extracting a core sample. Her partner, BENEDICT "BEN" ANGOLA (50s, tailored suit under a borrowed apron), holds a flashlight. A boy of twenty, CASPER TREMAINE-LIU (20s, security guard's cap), stands rooted at the tunnel mouth, jaw slack.

She taps a wheel. He lifts the lamp. She pulls out a plug. Inside, wrapped in wax paper, a slim steel tube.

MARISKA
There it is.

BEN
There it is.

CASPER
(approaching)
Hey. Hey, that's not allowed.

Mariska pockets the tube. Ben swings the lamp up. Casper stops and raises both hands, and they stare at one another across eight feet of fog.

CASPER (CONT'D)
(a little desperate)
I'm only the night guard.

BEN
We're only the night shift.

Mariska takes a wheel off the rack, hefts it, and rolls it down the tunnel. It gathers speed, thunders off into the dark. Casper turns to watch it go.

CASPER
That was a forty-year Gruyere.

MARISKA
Ben, go.

BEN
(at the same time)
Mariska, go.

They run. Casper lowers his hands, looks at the empty rack, and then, very slowly, at his own radio.
